    "https://www.cofo.edu/Academics/Career-Services": {
      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services | Academics | Hard Work U. Skip Navigation to Content Campusweb Keeter Center Ralph Foster Museum Lab School K-12 Campus Store Athletics Search Apply About Accolades & Accreditation Meet President Johnson and First Lady Laura Johnson Consumer Information Events & Community Programs Human Resources Hard Work U. News FAQs Admissions Virtual Tour Apply Request Information Admission Criteria Graduate Debt-Free Timeline & Interview Campus Life Cost & Financial Aid Counselor Tool Box Academics Majors & Minors Pre-Professional Resources Library College Catalog Student Handbook Registrar's Office Career Services Faithful Lives Pillars Academic Christian Cultural Patriotic Vocational Visit Welcome Video Sights to See Famous Visitors Campus Store The Keeter Center S of O Lab School Alumni Alumni Giving Join or Update Alumni News Alumni Chapters Meritorious Awards Request Transcript Lake Honor Restoration Project Give Give Online Associates Planned Giving Request Info PhilanthroCorp Estate Services Apply Search Academics - Career Services About Accolades & Accreditation Meet President Johnson and First Lady Laura Johnson Consumer Information Events & Community Programs Human Resources Hard Work U. News FAQs Admissions Virtual Tour Apply Request Information Admission Criteria Graduate Debt-Free Timeline & Interview Campus Life Cost & Financial Aid Counselor Tool Box Academics Majors & Minors Pre-Professional Resources Library College Catalog Student Handbook Registrar's Office Career Services Faithful Lives Pillars Academic Christian Cultural Patriotic Vocational Visit Welcome Video Sights to See Famous Visitors Campus Store The Keeter Center S of O Lab School Alumni Alumni Giving Join or Update Alumni News Alumni Chapters Meritorious Awards Request Transcript Lake Honor Restoration Project Give Give Online Associates Planned Giving Request Info PhilanthroCorp Estate Services Apply Campusweb Keeter Center Ralph Foster Museum Lab School K-12 Campus Store Athletics The Vocation Center is committed to student success, and assists students with academic major/minor selection and the development of professional pathways. Additionally, we offer assistance with career assessments, résumés, cover letters, LinkedIn, and developing interview skills. The Vocation Center also helps students find part-time jobs and internships that will help them gain the necessary experience for future employment. Coaching with the director is available by appointment. Vocation Center hours are Monday-Friday, 8:00 AM- 5:00 PM. Contact us at career@cofo.edu or 417-690-3248 Visit the FAQ s for more information. Want to hire our students? Send job descriptions directly to our office email: career@cofo.edu Temporary Jobs (i.e., babysitting, moving assistance, yard work) Please call or email us at 417-690-3248, career@cofo.edu Fall 2026 CAREER EXPO - September 23, 2026 (10:00 a.m. to 2:00 p.m.) Our Purpose We help students to understand the deep and rich biblical expression of \"Vocation\" and how to utilize this understanding through their \"Callings,” thus transitioning into the marketplace with a healthy, mission-minded approach. We love to hear our Alumni's success stories. Contact us and let us know about any major promotions and accomplishments so we can highlight you to our students! Summer & Seasonal job fair\r\n(Dates dropping soon) The annual Vocation Trip is an experience designed to help students explore their vocation and prepare for life after graduation. During the trip, students travel to a major city where they connect with alumni, business leaders, nonprofits, and organizations to gain career insight and professional experience. Students participate in networking opportunities, career development workshops, TED-style talks, and visits to businesses and community organizations while refining skills such as interviewing, résumé building, LinkedIn, and networking. The trip encourages students to discover their strengths, grow in confidence, and reflect on how their personal calling and career path align with their values and purpose. Vocation Center Director Candace Stark is the Director of the Vanek Center for Vocation and Callings at College of the Ozarks. She is deeply committed to serving students and dedicated to supporting their success in their academic, professional, and personal journeys.  Her professional mission is to equip the next generation with the knowledge, confidence, and tools needed to pursue their vocations and make meaningful contributions to their communities. She thrives on leading initiatives that prepare students for lives of impact, purpose, and service. Administrative Assistant Sarah Williams is the Administrative Assistant of the Vanek Center for Vocation and Callings. An alumna of College of the Ozarks, she is happy to build relationships and provide guidance to students who come looking for it as well as the ones she supervises at the Vanek Center. Student Associates Caleb Martin is a junior double-majoring in Marketing and Business Management and Savannah Mosher is a sophomore majoring in Psychology. Skip to Top of Page © 2026 College of the Ozarks Mailing Address: P.O. Box 17, Point Lookout, MO 65726 Physical Address: 1 Opportunity Ave., Point Lookout, MO 65726 Main Number: 1.800.222.0525 Contact Student Achievement Accessibility Terms Of Use Login"
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/7def0b94-1f28-4661-bf1e-1145b0065de9.pdf?ver=M7JGMf8SRzCk437-oRlGMA%3d%3d": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Computer Science",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Computer Science  \nCollege of the Ozarks invites applications for a full-time faculty position in Computer Science \nbeginning in the Fall 2027 semester, though starting Spring 2027 may be possible.  We seek a \nstudent-centered, self-motivated, and versatile faculty member with strong teaching skills and a \ndemonstrated ability to collaborate and communicate effectively with colleagues. This position \nwill focus primarily on the continued development and stewardship of our new Data Science \nand Artificial Intelligence program.  \nThe Computer Science Department offers majors and minors in Computer Information Science, \nComputer Science, and Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, as well as a minor in \nCybersecurity and a range of general education courses.  \nTeaching responsibilities will include both lower- and upper-division courses in Computer \nScience, Data Science, and Artificial Intelligence. The successful candidate will also be expected \nto maintain and develop course content and curriculum to ensure high-quality instruction and \nongoing alignment with academic standards and industry needs. The standard teaching load is \n24 credit hours over a nine-month academic year .  \nCollege of the Ozarks is a distinctive liberal arts, work-study college of approximately 1,450 \nstudents, located in southwest Missouri near Branson. Deeply rooted in Christian faith and \nservice, the College is known for its close-knit community, strong mentoring culture, and \ncommitment to developing students academically, professionally, and spiritually. Class sizes are \nintentionally small, typically 10 to 25 students in STEM courses, allowing faculty to build \nmeaningful relationships with students.  \nCollege of the Ozarks seeks faculty members who embrace the institution’s Christian mission, \ndemonstrate excellence in undergraduate teaching, serve as mentors and positive role models \nfor students, and contribute collaboratively to the life of the College. Applicants should hold an \nM.S., D.Sc., or Ph.D. in Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related computing field. \nCandidates with degrees in a related discipline should also demonstrate substantial, well-\ndocumented experience in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence.  \nTo apply, please submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, transcripts, and three letters of \nrecommendation, including one from your pastor, to Dr. Susan DeWoody, Provost, PO Box 17, \nPoint Lookout, MO 65726, or by email to provostoffice@cofo.edu. Review of applications will \nbegin immediately and continue until the position is filled. "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/a3883ee5-135e-4cb7-8caf-c9f4146ff953.pdf?ver=T36jCjetNKamvxeZnkgA9Q%3d%3d": {
      "title": "Christ-centered mission, pursue excellence in teaching undergraduate students, commit",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Agriculture/Biology/Chemistry/Computer Science/Physics \n College of the Ozarks invites applicants for part-time faculty member positions in the \nsciences. \n College of the Ozarks is committed to hiring faculty members who embrace the College’s \nChrist-centered mission, pursue excellence in teaching undergraduate students, commit \nto serving as a mentor and positive role model, and seek integration of their academic \ndiscipline and Christian faith. Faculty are expected to be self-motivated and versatile with \nstrong communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and \nstaff.  \nPrimary responsibilities for this position are developing and teaching undergraduate \nscience courses based on the candidate’s credentials and expertise. Preference will be \ngiven to candidates with credentials in agriculture, biology, chemistry, computer science, \nor physics.  \nCandidates should hold an M.S. in agriculture, chemistry, biology, computer science or the \nbasic sciences. A Ph.D. is preferred, as is undergraduate teaching experience. College of \nthe Ozarks is a small (1,450 students), liberal arts focused, work-study college with a \ncommitment to evangelical Christian faith and service, located in southwest Missouri near \nBranson (www.cofo.edu).  \nSend a letter of application and CV to Dr. Susan DeWoody, Provost, PO Box 17, Point \nLookout, MO 65726, or email provostoffice@cofo.edu. Review of applications begins \nimmediately, with placement dependent upon credentials and current course needs. "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/3d6f9544-8050-4605-a150-d1e6106d3d02.pdf?ver=fswfhs-g8XscIX5fAIBh8g%3d%3d": {
      "title": "College of the Ozarks seeks applicants for part-time faculty position in the department of",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Applied Nutrition \nCollege of the Ozarks seeks applicants for part-time faculty position in the department of \nApplied Nutrition.    \nPrimary responsibilities for this position are developing and teaching undergraduate \nnutrition courses based on the candidate’s credentials and expertise (potential areas \ninclude food production, cultural foods, foodservice management, sports nutrition, or \ncommunity nutrition).  \nCandidates should hold an M.S. in nutrition, food science, or a related area, or be \ncredentialed as a Registered Dietitian. A Ph.D. is preferred, as is undergraduate teaching \nexperience.  \nSuccessful candidates must embrace the College’s Christ-centered mission and \ndemonstrate excellence in teaching undergraduate students, a commitment to serving as \na mentor and positive role model, and an interest in the relationship of nutrition and \nChristian faith. College of the Ozarks is a small (1,400 students), liberal arts, work-study \ncollege with a commitment to evangelical Christian faith and service located in southwest \nMissouri near Branson (www.cofo.edu). To apply, please send a letter of application and \nCV to: Dr. Susan DeWoody, Provost, PO Box 17, Point Lookout, MO 65726, or email \nprovostoffice@cofo.edu. \n "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/9c5d8d94-fdab-43f6-bc4d-87b7bf300c15.pdf?ver=zWXyoMzUNi0siSLJcteeXw%3d%3d": {
      "title": "College of the Ozarks seeks applicants for a part-time faculty position in the department",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Chemistry/Biochemistry \nCollege of the Ozarks seeks applicants for a part-time faculty position in the department \nof Chemistry/Biochemistry for the fall semester of 2026. Primary responsibility for this \nposition will be teaching undergraduate organic chemistry lectures and laboratories. \nCandidates should hold at least an M.S. in chemistry, a Ph.D. is preferred, with \nundergraduate teaching experience.  \nSuccessful candidates must embrace the College’s Christ-centered mission and \ndemonstrate excellence in teaching undergraduate students, a commitment to serving \nas a mentor and positive role model, and an interest in the relationship of the natural \nsciences to Christian faith. College of the Ozarks is a small (1,400 students), liberal arts, \nwork-study college with a commitment to evangelical Christian faith and service, located \nin southwest Missouri near Branson (www.cofo.edu). To apply, please send a letter of \napplication and CV to: Dr. Susan DeWoody, Provost, PO Box 17, Point Lookout, MO \n65726, or email provostoffice@cofo.edu. "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/61ad8401-7dc7-41f4-a713-30627b003c05.pdf?ver=IKV9-Oaekuhew15v1gHa4g%3d%3d": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Engineering",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Engineering \nShape Future Engineers at College of the Ozarks! \nAre you a passionate engineering professional looking to make a real difference in students' lives? College of \nthe Ozarks is seeking dynamic part-time Adjunct Faculty members to teach in-person courses in the multi-\ndisciplinary engineering program in the James P . Keeter School of Engineering. \nWhat You'll Do: \n• Inspire and educate undergraduate students in engaging courses related to industrial/manufacturing, \nchemical, mechanical, or civil engineering (structures) \n• Bring your real-world experience to the classroom, making learning relevant and exciting \n• Serve as a mentor and positive role model, guiding students in their academic and professional \njourneys \n• Collaborate with a supportive team of faculty and staff who are dedicated to student success \nWhy College of the Ozarks? \nWe're more than just a college; we're a community rooted in Christian values and a commitment to \nexcellence. As an adjunct faculty member, you'll have the opportunity to: \n• Integrate your faith and professional expertise in a meaningful way \n• Work with highly motivated students who are eager to learn \n• Enjoy a beautiful campus environment and a close-knit community \nAre You a Good Fit? \nWe're looking for someone who is: \n• Committed to our Christian mission and values \n• Passionate about teaching and mentoring undergraduate students \n• Self-motivated and adaptable with strong communication skills \n• Able to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and industrial partners \nQualifications: \n• M.S. or Ph.D. in engineering OR  \n• M.S. in a relevant non-engineering field with significant, documented engineering experience OR \n• P .E. license OR \n• For select industrial engineering courses, a Lean Six Sigma Black Belt certification \nReady to Apply? \nIf you're ready to join a team that's shaping the next generation of hard-working versatile engineers, we \nencourage you to apply! Please send a letter of application and CV to: Dr. Susan DeWoody, Provost, PO Box \n17, Point Lookout, MO 65726, or email provostoffice@cofo.edu. "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/de551c6c-3dba-4694-80c3-54373a2a4f61.pdf?ver=SThaPnhlunly9F26CwV4Vg%3d%3d": {
      "title": "College of the Ozarks seeks applicants for part-time faculty position in political science.",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Political Science \nCollege of the Ozarks seeks applicants for part-time faculty position in political science. \nPrimary responsibilities for this position are developing and teaching undergraduate, \ngeneral education political science courses.  \nCandidates should hold a master’s degree in political science or similar discipline. A Ph.D. \nis preferred, as is undergraduate teaching experience. Successful candidates must \nembrace the College’s Christ-centered mission and demonstrate excellence in teaching \nundergraduate students, a commitment to serving as a mentor and positive role model, \nand an interest in the relationship of political science and Christian faith.  \nCollege of the Ozarks is a small (1,500 students), liberal arts, work-study college with a \ncommitment to evangelical Christian faith and service located in southwest Missouri near \nBranson (www.cofo.edu). To apply, please send a letter of application and CV to: Dr. Susan \nDeWoody, Provost, PO Box 17, Point Lookout, MO 65726, or email provostoffice@cofo.edu. "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/d06ac212-59b9-4e85-a3df-34efaff01479.pdf?ver=ZWed18fLetfpW2sMz2KVGQ%3d%3d": {
      "title": "College of the Ozarks invites applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position in Studio",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Studio Art \n \nCollege of the Ozarks invites applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position in Studio \nArt.  \n \nCollege of the Ozarks is committed to hiring faculty members who embrace the \ninstitution’s Christian mission, pursue excellence in teaching undergraduate students, and \nserve as mentors and positive role models. Faculty are expected to be self-motivated and \nversatile, with strong communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with other \nfaculty and staff. Primary responsibilities for this position include teaching undergraduate \nfoundational studio art courses such as Drawing I, 2D Design and Exploration of Visual Art.  \n \nCandidates should hold an M.F .A. or M.A. in Studio Art. A terminal degree is preferred, as is \nundergraduate teaching experience. College of the Ozarks is a Christian liberal arts college \nwith a commitment to faith-based education. The campus is in Point Lookout, MO near \nBranson. \n \nTo apply, please address a letter of application to Dr. Susan DeWoody and send the letter \nand CV to Andrea Oliver at provostoffice@cofo.edu. Review of applications begins \nimmediately, with placement dependent upon credentials and current course needs. \n "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/b66e4c6f-1526-404c-ba80-5f64939efd30.pdf?ver=Dvap8b_Bn3Ukb2FmlpMRRA%3d%3d": {
      "title": "College of the Ozarks invites applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position in Theatre.",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Theatre \nCollege of the Ozarks invites applicants for a part-time adjunct faculty position in Theatre.  \nCollege of the Ozarks is committed to hiring faculty members who embrace the \ninstitution’s Christian mission, pursue excellence in teaching undergraduate students, and \nserve as mentors and positive role models. Faculty are expected to be self-motivated and \nversatile, with strong communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with \nother faculty and staff. Primary responsibilities for this position include teaching \nundergraduate foundational theatre courses such as Exploration of Theatre, Movement \nand Vocal Training for the Stage, and Introduction to Technical Theatre.    \nCandidates should hold an M.F.A. or M.A. in Theatre. A terminal degree is preferred, as is \nundergraduate teaching experience. College of the Ozarks is a Christian liberal arts college \nwith a commitment to faith-based education. The campus is in Point Lookout, MO, near \nBranson. \nTo apply, please address a letter of application to Dr. Susan DeWoody and send the letter \nand CV to Andrea Oliver at provostoffice@cofo.edu. Review of applications begins \nimmediately, with placement dependent upon credentials and current course needs. \n "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/e3a52c4c-2c93-4875-9cdf-a2388762b6fe.pdf?ver=8zY66Qqmv3JYCMNuTMPHWw%3d%3d": {
      "title": "College of the Ozarks invites applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position in",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Applied Music \n College of the Ozarks invites applicants for a part-time, adjunct faculty position in \ninstrumental private lesson instruction.  \nCollege of the Ozarks is committed to hiring faculty members who embrace the \ninstitution’s Christian mission, pursue excellence in teaching undergraduate students, and \nserve as mentors and positive role models. Faculty are expected to be self-motivated and \nversatile, with strong communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with other \nfaculty and staff. Primary responsibilities for this position include teaching private lessons \nin woodwinds, brass, guitar, or percussion, as well as instructing a methods class suited to \nthe instructor’s particular area of expertise. \nCandidates should hold a master’s degree in music and/or possess considerable \nperformance experience. Undergraduate teaching experience is a plus. College of the \nOzarks is a Christian liberal arts college with a commitment to faith-based education. The \ncampus is in Point Lookout, MO, near Branson.  \nTo apply, please address a letter of application to Dr. Susan DeWoody and send the letter \nand CV to Andrea Oliver at provostoffice@cofo.edu. Review of applications begins \nimmediately, with placement dependent upon credentials and current course needs. "
    },
    "https://www.cofo.edu/Portals/0/Accolades/b3420b80-58db-4df3-97b3-b34edf983881.pdf?ver=FwDCil_hb8C0wwCIhVdZaA%3d%3d": {
      "title": "Part-Time Adjunct Instructor in Music — Strings (Violin, Viola, & Cello)",
      "description": "Part-Time Adjunct Instructor in Music — Strings (Violin, Viola, & Cello) \n \nCollege of the Ozarks (C of O) is seeking applications for a part-time adjunct instructor of \nstrings to teach in-person applied lessons and string-related music courses in the C of O \nmusic department. We are seeking an energetic musician with strong communication skills, \nsubstantial teaching experience, and a broad knowledge of string instruments. \n \nPrimary Teaching Responsibilities \n• Applied lessons on violin, viola, & cello (approximately 10–15 students each week) \n• Instrumental Methods-Strings: a laboratory course designed to teach the pedagogy and \nliterature of the string family of instruments through practical application and illustration \n• Instrumental Ensemble: performance of classical chamber music by an instrumental \nensemble of 3 to 8 players \n \nAdditional Responsibilities \n• Oversee the maintenance of the music department’s string instruments and related  \nequipment \n \nMinimum Qualifications \n• A bachelor’s degree in music \n• Applied string teaching experience (violin; minimum of five years) \n• Ensemble performance experience \n \nPreferred Qualifications \n• A master’s or doctorate degree in music \n• Applied string teaching experience at the college level (violin, viola, & cello) \n• Classroom teaching experience at the college level \n• Ensemble leadership experience \n• Experience maintaining string instruments and related equipment \n \nCollege of the Ozarks is a Christian liberal arts-based college with a commitment to faith-\nbased education. The campus is in Point Lookout, MO, near Branson. To apply, please \naddress a letter of application to Dr. Susan DeWoody and send the letter and CV to Andrea \nOliver at provostoffice@cofo.edu. Review of applications begins immediately, with \nplacement dependent upon credentials and current course needs. "
    },
